 # --- BERLIN KILLINGS ---
 ("59","But Wiessee was only the beginning. In Berlin, Göring and Himmler had unleashed the lists.","IMG",["Hermann Göring Berlin 1934","Goering command 1934"],"slow-push","cut"),
 ("60","At the Cadet School in Lichterfelde, 150 storm troopers were lined against a wall and cut down by firing squads.","IMG",["Lichterfelde cadet school Berlin","Kadettenanstalt Lichterfelde"],"slow-push","xfade"),
 ("61","Among them Karl Ernst, the Berlin S.A. leader, dragged from his honeymoon, shouting Heil Hitler to the end.","IMG",["Karl Ernst SA Berlin","Karl Ernst storm trooper"],"slow-pull","xfade"),
 ("62","But the guns did not stop at the S.A. S.S. men rang the doorbell of General von Schleicher.","IMG",["Kurt von Schleicher general portrait","Schleicher 1934"],"slow-push","xfade"),
 ("63","When Schleicher opened his own front door, they shot him dead. His wife stepped forward — they shot her too.","IMG",["Schleicher villa Berlin","1930s Berlin villa"],"slow-push","xfade"),
 ("64","Gregor Strasser, once the second man in the party, was seized and shot in his cell on Göring's order.","IMG",["Gregor Strasser Nazi","Gregor Strasser portrait"],"slow-pull","dip-to-black"),
 ("65","Papen survived only by luck, under house arrest, while the S.S. gutted his office and murdered his staff.","IMG",["Franz von Papen 1934 portrait","Papen vice chancellor"],"slow-push","cut"),
 ("66","Then the old grudges. Gustav von Kahr, who crushed the 1923 putsch, was found in a swamp, hacked to death.","IMG",["Gustav von Kahr","Kahr Bavaria 1923"],"slow-push","xfade"),
 ("67","A priest who once helped edit Mein Kampf was found in a forest, his neck broken, three bullets in his heart.","IMG",["Bavarian forest 1930s","German woodland dark"],"slow-pull","xfade"),
 ("68","And a music critic named Willi Schmid was taken from his cello while his children played — killed by mistake for a man with a similar name.","IMG",["cello 1930s study","1930s music room"],"slow-push","dip-to-black"),

